---
fmContentType: glossaryEntry
term: "CBDA (Cannabidiolic Acid)"
letter: "C"
anchor: "cbda"
category: "cannabinoids"
---

The raw, acidic precursor to CBD found in unheated cannabis. Like THCA converting to THC, CBDA converts to CBD through decarboxylation — applying heat over time. Raw cannabis contains mostly CBDA, not CBD. Decarbing is required to activate it for edibles.

→ [How to Decarb Cannabis](/edibles/decarb-activate-cannabis-edibles/)
